From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:10:48 +0200
Subject: LLInt: load the callee as a whole slot under JSVALUE64

getVMFromCallFrame, used on every exception unwind, read the callee with 'loadp Callee + PayloadOffset[cfr]' when WebAssembly is off: harmless where PayloadOffset is 0, but on 64-bit big-endian (ppc64, s390x: C_LOOP builds without WebAssembly) PayloadOffset is 4, so it loaded half the callee pointer and half the next slot, and the VM lookup from that crashed. Every caught exception killed the process: try { null.x } catch {} in jsc, Wikipedia in the browser. op_super_construct's callee cache had the same offset. Under JSVALUE64 both now load the whole slot.

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.asm b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.asm
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.asm
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/LowLevelInterpreter.asm
@@ -1617,7 +1617,13 @@ if WEBASSEMBLY
         loadp JSWebAssemblyInstance::m_vm[vm], vm
     .loaded:
 else
-    loadp Callee + PayloadOffset[cfr], vm
+    # The callee is a whole 64-bit slot under JSVALUE64: PayloadOffset (4 on big-endian) is for
+    # 32-bit values only.
+    if JSVALUE64
+        loadp Callee[cfr], vm
+    else
+        loadp Callee + PayloadOffset[cfr], vm
+    end
     convertJSCalleeToVM(vm)
 end
 end
@@ -2603,7 +2609,7 @@ commonCallOp(op_super_construct, OpSuperConstruct, prepareForRegularCall, invoke
         lshifti 3, t1
         negp t1
         addp cfr, t1
-        loadp ThisArgumentOffset + PayloadOffset[t1], t1
+        loadp ThisArgumentOffset[t1], t1
         loadp OpSuperConstruct::Metadata::m_cachedCallee[t5], t2
         bqeq t1, t2, .done
         btqz t2, .store
